      "expectedShape": "\"connections\": { \"mcp\": [{ \"appSlug\": \"<marketplace slug>\", \"name\": \"<app name>\", \"userAppInstallations\": [{ \"id\": \"<installation ulid>\", \"name\": \"<app name>\" }] }] }  // multiple MCPs in one AI_TASK rarely makes sense; consider splitting"
    },
    "ai_task_scheduling_missing_date_tools": {
      "docRef": "node-specs/AI_TASK.md",
      "expectedShape": "\"connections\": { \"tools\": [{ \"name\": \"get_current_date_time\", \"external\": false, \"operationParameters\": { \"get_current_date_time\": { \"timezone\": { \"mode\": \"value\", \"value\": \"<IANA zone of the business>\" } } } }, { \"name\": \"get_weekday_of_a_date\", \"external\": false }] }  // required when the node connects a scheduling app (Google Calendar, Calendly, ...): an error when the app is recognised exactly (connections.mcp[].appSlug or an installation slug from the marketplace list, or a name that spells the app, e.g. \"Google Calendar\"), a warning when only a word of the name looks like a calendar (\"Booking status API\"); `jelou workflow validate --fix` adds the tools in both cases and pins the zone it finds in the file: a pin another AI_TASK already has (a template or UTC included), else a \"Zona horaria / Time zone / Fuso horário: <IANA>\" line in a prompt (markdown allowed), kept as the author spelled it; with no zone, or two different ones, it pins nothing: pin it yourself (Business time zone in node-specs/AI_TASK.md)"
    },
